A||||5||Cheever2||Patting myself on the back||||10||
Z||000000||Cheever2||05-17-2001||03:45 PM||||Hey guys, I just finished replacing my headliner - all by myself!  It's not perfect, but very close.  I don't know how you can prevent having a few wrinkles around the edge.  Took a lot of time and buckets of sweat (already hot here - hence my desire for A/C in the garage), but it's done in time for the FieroFest in Oklahoma City.  I <B>should</B> have used that time to replace the front brake pads, but judges don't look at those, lol.  <P>Somebody needs to redesign how the interior trim pieces attach.  Grrr...<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000001||FieroLisa||05-17-2001||03:55 PM||||I feel your pain on the interior trim pieces- Those dang pillars....GRRR is all I have to say. I thought I had it all put together, but then had to keep taking it apart for stupid small reasons.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||05-17-2001||04:50 PM||||Since I am the first person to ever take the sunroof out of my 85se, and I love to drive it around in windblast mode, i will be doing my headliner in the not too distant future.<P>I tried putting some glue behind it to slow down the process, but 'shes breaking up, Captain'<P>maybe fabric is not the way to go. Oak paneling maybe?<P> okay okay! just kidding!||||reg||1
Z||000003||mbramble||05-17-2001||04:54 PM||||I found the hardest part of replacing the headliner was getting the ?&gt;(*& sun visors put back in!!  Of course mine were in a project car and had been twisted all around fom the way they originally came out.  What a pain!!<P>Another headliner pain -- I just put a sunroof on my project car and the only headliner I had available was badly damaged and from a solid roof car!!  I repaired the damage with fiberglass and cut the hole and then covered it.  It fits!!  But, what a pain!!<P>Good job Cheever, give 'em heck at the show!!<P>Lisa, I have learned that no matter how many times you think you are finished and can go ahead and put the trim back on, you will always find one other reason to take it off!!  On this project car, I had the entire interior out, I mean everything was out but the ECM and the main wiring harnesses.  I figured I would get all the wiring done that I needed to before putting anything back in.  Once it was, I put the carpet back in and then the dash and guages.  As soon as I had the blasted dash guages remounted I found that I needed to make one more wiring change!!  Had to pull it back out again.  And probably will 10 more times before the car is put on the road!!<P>Mike<BR><p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 05-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||WKDFIRO||05-19-2001||12:56 AM||||Pat on the back for you! <P>I would not be so brave when my sunroof cloth comes down. I think I would scream like a girl and have a professional do it!<P>Yeah Im ashamed but at least Im honest!||||reg||11
Z||000005||tgowens||05-19-2001||02:04 AM||||I install headliners all the time and all I can tell you is that it gets easier every time you do it. But then, when you only need to do it once and haven't before I guess it <I>is</I> a pain.......(remembering the first one I did.......) -- <P>I would like to mention this though - if any of you re-do your headliner and use the molded fiberglass headliner board, make the proper cut-outs (I use a Dremel) and check the fit several times before you cover it with the fabric (I have found that the pre-marked clothes hook locations are almost 1 1/2 inches off! - measure it yourself in spite of the fact that the board may be pre-marked!. Allow for about a 1/16" as the foam backed headliner material adds to the thickness. When you cover the headliner board you can trim flush on the right and left sides but leave an overlap on the front and rear. Cut and or drill holes before you install it and all should be well when you do.<P>Oh, one more thing, it always helps me if I support the headliner with the mirror, install the clothes hangers, then the dome light and finally the visors. I always mark the visor holes with a pencil when removing them (F=front, R=Rear and I=the inside (closest to the mirror) hole of the left visor - the right visor obviously only needs the F and R marks......) - it works for me every time.......<P>A pat on the back for you and a good luck at the show too!!<P>------------------<BR>My Fiero Web Site.....<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tgowens.gif">               </A><P>87 GT - 2.8L Gold automatic<BR>87 GT - 2.8L Blue automatic<BR>87 GT - 3.4L Blue 5-speed Getrag<BR>87 GT - 2.8L Med. Red Met. 5-speed Getrag<BR>88 Coupe - 2.5L Red automatic<p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 05-19-2001).]||||reg||1
